# docs/2026-07-08/ — presentation working folder.
#
# Track the human-authored deliverables (LaTeX + the final figures we reference), and
# IGNORE the bulky/derived/scratch artifacts that don't belong in git history.
#
# What we KEEP (NOT ignored — see negations at the bottom):
#   presentation.tex        the Overleaf source
#   *.md                    explainer notes (e.g. concept writeups)
#   figures/*.png|*.svg      the exact figures the .tex references
#
# What we IGNORE (below):

# --- Raw run data / pools (large, live on the HPC clusters, re-derivable) ------------------
*.npz            # sampled bitstring pools / per-step recovery arrays (10s of MB each)
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.fcidump
fcidump_*        # integral dumps staged for reference calcs

# --- Scratch JSON / CSV telemetry copied down for plotting (source of truth is on-cluster) --
runs/            # any local mirror of the cluster runs/ tree
localfigs/       # scratch figure-rendering staging dir
refs.json
*_refs.json
energies.csv
recovery_trace*.json

# --- LaTeX build products (regenerated by Overleaf / latexmk) ------------------------------
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.bbl
*.blg
*.nav
*.snm
*.vrb

# --- OS / editor cruft ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp

# --- Negations: force-track the deliverables even though patterns above might catch them ----
!presentation.tex
!*.md
!figures/
!figures/*.png
!figures/*.svg
